  "entity_source.invalid_details": "**Check selected sources**\n\n{fields}. These assignments do not match the requirements above. Open each entity row and choose a matching search result.",
  "entity_source.pending_details": "**Source check incomplete**\n\nThe editor does not yet have all required information for: {fields}. Open the entity search to load the source metadata. Missing information alone does not mean the entity is unsuitable.",
  "entity_source.price_help": "**Price series**\n\nChoose the sensor that provides a dated list of electricity prices, for example the integration’s Price series entity. A single current price, an average or a CO₂ reading is not a price forecast. The entity search offers supported series only.\n\n**Supported data**\n\nThe source must supply time/price rows in a supported data or raw_today/raw_tomorrow list. Raw EUR or cent prices per Wh, kWh or MWh are converted to EUR/kWh. The dates must cover the displayed period; missing intervals remain gaps.\n\n**Average reference (optional)**\n\nA secondary sensor in EUR/kWh or €/kWh supplies the reference average. It takes precedence over the fixed average in this section. Without either reference, the widget uses the displayed series’ average.\n\n**If no prices appear**\n\nCheck the selected entity’s attributes and timestamps in Home Assistant, then reopen its entity search. Choose the list sensor, rather than a similarly named current-price or CO₂ sensor.",
  "entity_source.parqet_help": "**Portfolio amounts**\n\nTotal value, unrealised gain and dividends need Monetary sensors. This device class does not distinguish portfolio value from fees or taxes: choose the corresponding financial metric of the same portfolio and interval.\n\n**Returns**\n\nXIRR and unrealised return need percentage sensors without a physical device class. Battery or humidity percentages are not returns.\n\n**Portfolio details**\n\nThe total-value sensor must also provide the integration’s portfolio and holding attributes for period requests and positions. A Monetary class alone does not supply these details.",
